<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 15 August, from 718 to 1947.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">718 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,308 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Umayyad army abandons its siege of Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Umayyad army under Maslama ibn Abd al-Malik withdrew from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> with heavy losses after a year-long siege by land and sea. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-iii-the-isaurian">Emperor Leo III</a>'s defenders had been helped by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-fire">Greek fire</a>, a harsh winter and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgar</a> attacks.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-arab-siege-of-constantinople">Second Arab siege of Constantinople</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/778">778 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,248 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Basques destroy Charlemagne's rearguard at Roncevaux</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Basque fighters ambushed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s rearguard in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>, killing the commander Roland. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> of Roland later recast the skirmish as a heroic stand against Saracens.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basques">Basques</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1057">1057 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">969 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Macbeth is killed at the Battle of Lumphanan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Macbeth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> was killed at Lumphanan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aberdeenshire">Aberdeenshire</a> by forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malcolm-iii-of-scotland">Malcolm Canmore</a>, Duncan's son. He had ruled for 17 years and even made a pilgrimage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1209">1209 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">817 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Cathar stronghold of Carcassonne falls to the crusaders</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege that began on 1 August, the fortified town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carcassonne">Carcassonne</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/languedoc">Languedoc</a> surrendered to the crusaders led by Arnaud Amaury. Under the negotiated surrender its inhabitants were allowed to leave free of harm.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catharism">Catharism</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1224 CE <span class="tih-ago">802 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Livonian Brothers of the Sword capture Tartu</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a>, an order of German crusading knights, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tartu">Tartu</a>, or Dorpat, the last major centre of Estonian resistance on the mainland. It became the seat of the Bishopric of Dorpat.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tartu">Tartu</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-crusade">Livonian Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1534">1534 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">492 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ignatius of Loyola and companions take vows at Montmartre</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ignatius and six companions vowed poverty and chastity in a chapel on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montmartre">Montmartre</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. The group became the Society of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a>, approved by the Pope in 1540.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1769">1769 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">257 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon Bonaparte is born in Corsica</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Napoleone Buonaparte was born in Ajaccio, a year after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> acquired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corsica">Corsica</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>. He rose to become Emperor of the French and redrew the map and laws of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corsica">Corsica</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Hirohito broadcasts Japan's surrender</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">For the first time, ordinary Japanese heard their emperor's voice as he announced acceptance of the Allied terms. The day is marked as VJ Day in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>; the formal surrender was signed on 2 September.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hirohito">Hirohito</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1947">1947 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">79 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">India becomes independent as British rule ends</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At midnight <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> became independent, a day after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>. Partition uprooted perhaps 15 million people and communal violence killed hundreds of thousands, possibly up to two million.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 15 August <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-ix-of-leon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfonso-ix-of-leon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfonso IX of León</span><span class="tp">1171–1230</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albert-ballin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albert-ballin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albert Ballin</span><span class="tp">1857–1918</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ivan-mestrovic"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ivan-mestrovic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ivan Meštrović</span><span class="tp">1883–1962</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/arnulfo-arias"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/arnulfo-arias.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Arnulfo Arias</span><span class="tp">1901–1988</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/oscar-romero"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/oscar-romero.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Óscar Romero</span><span class="tp">1917–1980</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 15 August <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/altfrid"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Altfrid</span><span class="tp">d. 874</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/li-yu-southern-tang"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/li-yu-southern-tang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Li Yu (Southern Tang)</span><span class="tp">937–978</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/macbeth-king-of-scotland"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Macbeth, King of Scotland</span><span class="tp">c. 1005–1057</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/philippa-of-hainaut"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philippa-of-hainaut.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Philippa of Hainaut</span><span class="tp">c. 1310–1369</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rene-magritte"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rene-magritte.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">René Magritte</span><span class="tp">1898–1967</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sheikh-mujibur-rahman"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sheikh-mujibur-rahman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sheikh Mujibur Rahman</span><span class="tp">1920–1975</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
